  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSum = Rs. 18000\n\nAmount = Rs. 21780\n\nTime = 2 years\n\n**Concept used:**\n\nA = P(1 + r/100)t\n\nI = P(1 + r/100)t - P\n\nHere,\n\nA = amount\n\nP = principal and sum\n\nr = rate\n\nt = time\n\nI = interest\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nLet the rate of interest be r\n\nSo,\n\n21780 = 18000(1 + r/100)²\n\n⇒ 21780/18000 = (1 + r/100)2\n\n⇒ 1089/900 = (1 + r/100)2\n\n⇒ (33/30)² = (1 + r/100)2\n\n⇒ 33/30 = (1 + r/100)\n\n⇒ 33/30 = [(100 + r)/100]\n\n⇒ 3300 = 3000 + 30r\n\n⇒ 30r = 300\n\n⇒ r = 300/30\n\n⇒ r = 10\n\nSo, rate of interest = 10%\n\nNew rate = 15%\n\nSo,\n\nI = 18000(1 + 15/100)² - 18000\n\n⇒ I = 18000(1 + 3/20)2 - 18000\n\n⇒ I = 18000[(20 + 3)/20]2 - 18000\n\n⇒ I = 18000[(23/20]2 - 18000\n\n⇒ I = 18000 × (529/400) - 18000\n\n⇒ I = 23805 - 18000\n\n⇒ I = 5805\n\nSo, interest for the new rate = Rs. 5805\n\n**∴ Required compound interest is Rs. 5805.**",
